  "evidence": "Distinctive 2019 UK Conservative manifesto pledges appear throughout: “Get Brexit Done” timetable (no extension beyond Dec 2020), FTAs with US/AUS/NZ/Japan and up to 10 freeports; no rises in main income tax/NI/VAT rates and raising the NI threshold to £9,500; 50,000 more nurses; 6,000 more GPs and 50m more GP appointments; 40 new hospitals; 20,000 extra police; Australian-style points-based immigration; end ‘no‑fault’ evictions; target 300,000 homes a year; gigabit broadband nationwide by 2025 with £5bn for hard‑to‑reach areas; SME R&D tax credit to 13% and a new high‑risk research agency; leave the Common Fisheries Policy; Environment Bill with a new watchdog, 40GW offshore wind by 2030, fracking moratorium, £500m Blue Planet Fund; repeal the Fixed-term Parliaments Act, voter ID; exceed NATO 2% with 0.5% real growth; maintain 0.7% aid and introduce Magnitsky sanctions; tougher animal welfare laws and ban on trophy hunting imports.",
